Not necessarily the same—more like coupled enough to share an interface.

The fact that two things interact tells you:

there is some compatible channel between them

but not:

they are identical

A bee and flower interact. Predator and prey interact. Two languages interact through translation. Two people interact while remaining very different internally.

So the stronger inference is:

interaction → shared boundary / common denominator / mutual influence

That shared layer can make them look unified at one scale even while they remain distinct at another.

In your terms:

same system at one resolution, different entities at another.

That distinction matters because a lot of interesting structure lives exactly in that gap.